<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Notification small icon.

  Android renders notification small icons using ONLY the alpha channel: every
  non-transparent pixel is drawn in one system colour. So this must be a flat
  silhouette on transparent, never the full-colour mark.

  Same two-sole shape as PamojaMark and the launcher icon, generated from that
  same geometry rather than redrawn, so the three cannot drift apart. Each sole
  is drawn as the union of 15 overlapping circles shrinking heel to toe,
  the identical construction the Compose mark paints, at a lower circle count
  because 24dp cannot resolve more.

  Tread marks are deliberately omitted: at 24dp they close up into noise, and
  alpha-only rendering would flatten them into the silhouette anyway.
-->
